sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: the proof runner inside stage 3 of the command development pipeline (design: reference/verification-cases). One shared runner executes the cases of a command; a case is a specification built from a fixed set of steps. Orbit's own Swamp runs the runner over SSH in the task VM, as part of the "Run the proof" child of proof:run. The Gateway only admits the request and records the verdicts.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline stage 3 · proof runner
  %% kind: pipeline.3-proof-runner
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  %% lane NT icon=server pill=fleet tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>verify workflow
  participant VM as Task VM<br/>runner · over ssh
  participant NT as Nested fleet<br/>Gateway · 2 Nodes
  GW->>SW: Start the verify run<br/>cases · commit
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the commit and the commands whose cases `proof:run` selected
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the Gateway only authorizes; Swamp owns the run and its state
  SW->>VM: Select the cases<br/>runner plan
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the cases file of each selected command at the tested commit
  %%> - refuses a case with an unknown step, an unknown chart path or no batch
  %%> - lists the chart paths, options and codes that no case covers
  %%> - groups the cases by batch, in the order of the batch list; inside a batch, in file order
  VM-->>SW: Ordered plan<br/>batches · cases
  loop each batch, one at a time
    opt after the first batch
      SW->>VM: Reset the fleet<br/>workflow: proof-fleet-reset
      %%> Why:
      %%> - the first batch starts on the fresh fleet that the run made
      %%> - a later batch needs its own starting state, so the fleet returns to the ready copies
    end
    SW->>VM: Set up the batch<br/>batch setup steps
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - runs the setup steps of the batch, such as extra addresses on the Nodes
    %%> - does nothing for a batch without setup steps
    loop each case, one at a time
      SW->>VM: Run one case<br/>runner case ID
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - records the baseline: firewall rules, Gateway records, open listeners
      %%> - runs the setup, act and expect steps of the case in order
      %%> Result:
      %%> - one verdict line; the full receipt stays in the evidence directory
      VM->>NT: Set up the case<br/>listener · ufw_rule · probe
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - builds the starting state, then probes it, for example a blocked port and a working control port
      %%> - every created thing registers its undo
      %%> When:
      %%> - a failed setup step ends the case as `unrun`; it is not a pass
      VM->>NT: Run the real CLI<br/>built from the commit
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - the `act` steps call the command through its real interface and check exit status, result code and skip reason
      VM->>NT: Check the effect<br/>probe · ufw · record · doctor
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - the `expect` steps check traffic, rule order, the Gateway record and Doctor
      %%> - every step runs, so one verdict lists all failures
      VM->>NT: Clean up, compare<br/>undo stack · baseline
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - undoes what the case created, last first, even after a failure
      %%> - compares the fleet with the baseline; a difference is residue
      alt nothing left behind
        VM-->>SW: Verdict<br/>one JSON line
        %%> Returns:
        %%> - the case id, `passed` or `failed`, the cause, the failed step and the seconds
      else residue or failed cleanup
        VM--xSW: Verdict failed, dirty<br/>residue named
        SW->>VM: Reset the fleet<br/>before the next case
        %%> Why:
        %%> - this is the only reset inside a batch
      end
    end
  end
  alt every case passed
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>verdicts + receipt
    Note over GW: Record the result once<br/>PASS
  else a case failed or did not run
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed cases
    Note over GW: Record the result once<br/>FAIL
  end
